               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 76-year-old male patient, admitted on 13th December 2025 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray excluding pneumonia or pneumothorax, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 14th December 2025 in stable condition with oral prednisolone taper and inhaler optimisation. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Discharge medications and further recommendations are enclosed.</div>
               </text>
